Minimal repro (2026-09-30, target/debug/jet at 542012fe9 and the pre-#3856 build):

enum E {
    MissingSeparator(String)
    EmptyHalf(String)
    ProviderFirst(raw: String, replacement: String)
    NonCanonical(raw: String, replacement: String)
    RetiredNixpkgs(raw: String, replacement: String)
}
fn run() { print("hi") }

jet check: ~1 s. jet run: 1 variant ~4 s, 2 variants ~9 s, 5 variants > 60 s (no output; the 10-variant Jetpack RefError ran > 900 s). jet run --interpret: > 60 s. jet build: 100 s, prints hi. The enum is never used; time grows with variant count, so a shared post-check stage (TIR/MIR lowering, derive/auto-impl generation, or JIT/interp preparation) is exponential or high-order polynomial in variants. Blocks every Jetpack run/test (Jetpack has many such #Error enums) and likely the >3500 s #3676 unit run. Proof when fixed: the repro and a 30-variant version run in under 2 s on check, jet run, --interpret and AOT; add a golden example.

Owner ruling in chat, 2026-09-30: with `result: &Res` and `result.session: Session?`, the user writes

    if &result.session == { .Val(s) -> bump(&s.machine) }

Matching on a write window (`&place`) makes the payload bindings write windows into the matched place (like Rust `if let Some(s) = &mut x`); sema checks exclusivity and aliasing as for other write windows. Chosen over Optional.take(). Blocks about 60 errors in Compiler/JetEval (46 E0111, about 13 E0211). Implement in both compilers, all tiers, with a golden and UI snapshots. Repro: ~/.cache/jet-test-scratch/SelfHostBackend3/repro/win.jet.

Probe (2026-10-02, jet run, debug build of HEAD with cap-lints): a scope guard that tests a `done := false` flag runs its cleanup on success too.

```jet
fn save(fail: Bool) -> Int SaveError! {
    done := false
    _g :: scope.guard(() -> {
        if !done -> print("remove half-written report.tmp")
    })
    print("write report.tmp")
    if fail -> return Err(SaveError.Disk)
    done = true
    Ok(1)
}
```

Output on the success path still prints `remove half-written report.tmp`. This follows the capture law: an escaping lambda copies Copy values at creation (Docs/spec/spec.md:714-718). The trap is that `done = true` is silently invisible to the guard, and `jet check` reports no problem. Zig's errdefer and D's scope(failure) exist because this flag pattern is the usual workaround, so users will write it.

Related: D-DEFER-FAIL1 (#4201) ballots a failure-only guard; #2845 covers AOT lowering of escaping closures that mutate their own copy (a different defect).

Found 2026-10-03 by the runtime port (RtW1-GC-1 via RuntimeLead-1). Generic modules parameterized by a provider type fail when specialized. 22-line repro ~/.cache/jet-test-scratch/RtW1-GC-1/RUNTIME-GC-1/seam-module/unit.jet (`~/.cache/jet-luna/laneS.sh env SAFE_JET_MEM=3G ~/.cache/jet-luna/safe-jet.sh test unit.jet`, exit 1):
- E0611 'Native' undefined inside a concrete (specialized) function at line 14, though the module parameter N: Native is in scope;
- E0119 on the qualified impl `impl Provider.Native` at line 16;
- E0901 at line 10: strong_count demands a generated M8ConcreteNative instead of the source bound N: Native (the template bound rewrite fails).
This is the existing-surface route for the GC seam (no new syntax); the runtime GC policy port is blocked on it. Fix in both compilers with a golden.

Minimal repro (27 lines): ~/.cache/jet-test-scratch/Main-4481/enum_static_all.jet

enum Lang {
    C
    Go
    fn all() -> [Lang] Never! { [Lang]{Lang.C, Lang.Go} }
    fn root(self) -> String Never! { if self == { .C -> "c"  .Go -> "go" } }
    fn from_root(root: String) -> Lang? Never! {
        loop language in Lang.all() {
            if language.root() == root -> return Val(language)
        }
        None
    }
}
fn run() { print(Lang.from_root("go") != None); print(Lang.from_root("x") == None) }

`jet run` (target-rel3/release/jet, 2026-10-03 01:18, 3G cap) exits 101: internal compiler error: checked TIR cannot lower to MIR at 297..300: Lang::from_root: closure method without a checked operation (bytes 297..300 = `all` in `Lang.all()`), at Source/lib.rs:263. Expected output: true / true. Violates I2/I3 (sema accepted the call but recorded no checked operation for the self-less enum function used from another method of the same enum). Found porting Jetpack Lock (ForeignLanguage::from_root over ForeignLanguage.all(), JP-LOCK-PARSE full closure).

