**Owner directive (2026-10-20):** 1:1 parity before any Rust is removed, so no ported work is forgotten. Do not start before Track B (owner order A → B → C → E → D); this card must be ready.

**Ledger (committed, machine-readable; it is the deletion manifest):**
1. **Items.** Every Rust fn, type and impl method in Source/, crates/ and Compiler/Bootstrap/*.rs (~1.93M lines, ~68.8k functions on 2026-10-20) maps to a Jet item. Mapping sources, in order:
   - `// Rust: path:line` port comments;
   - name and module correspondence;
   - origin/port/main.

   Each row carries one status:
   - ported;
   - ported-differs (the difference stated);
   - not-ported;
   - dropped (reason: retired syntax, the Rust-emit backend, Rust-only glue). **Dropped rows go to the owner.**
2. **Tests.** Every Rust #[test] (10,290) maps to a Jet #Test / fn test, an Examples golden or a tests/ui fixture that runs on the Jet compiler, or to an owner-reviewed retirement.
3. **Coverage.** `jet test` with coverage (B4 adds the mode) proves every ported function executes.
4. **CLI.** Every jet, jetpack and jetos command and flag (cli-census) dispatches to Jet; there are zero jet_cli_not_ported surfaces (36 on 2026-10-20).

**Gate:** milestone e11-m02-rust-exit cannot close, and no Rust file may be deleted, while any row is unexplained.

**Existing parity cards feed this ledger:** #3881 #3893 #3898 #3908 #3913 #3917 #3919 #3924 #3942 #3961 #3983 #4262 #4115 #3590 #3690.

