Found by the Jetpack port (#3590, PkgModelFinish, Opus 5.5); reproduced by the lead with target/debug/jet built 2026-09-26 03:05. Command: systemd-run --user --scope --quiet --expand-environment=no -p MemoryMax=4G -p MemorySwapMax=0 timeout 300 target/debug/jet run src/<file>.jet (from the repro directory; package.jet beside src/). Repro ~/.cache/jet-luna/PkgModelFinish/defects/E-split-once-tuple/src/split.jet:

fn split_assign(text: String) -> ?(before: String, after: String) {
    text.split_once("=")
}

jet run: E0108 "This needs ?(after: String, before: String), but the value is ?(before: String, after: String)". Named-tuple identity seems to depend on field order in one place and on sorted order in another; the declared type and split_once's type are the same set of named fields.
